The attached image (Fig. 7D) is a Western blot that verifies the size and presence of both pro-IL-1β and active IL-1β in cell lysates and supernatants of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). It shows that LPS priming induces pro-IL-1β (∼30 kD) in cell lysates, while Nano-11 in combination with LPS priming leads to the cleavage and secretion of active IL-1β (∼17 kD) into the supernatant, confirming the ELISA results that indicate Nano-11, particularly when cells are primed with LPS, induces the secretion of the biologically active form of IL-1β.